.TH L3TOL 3 
.UC 2
.SH NAME
l3tol, ltol3 \- convert between 3-byte and long integers (2BSD)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
l3tol(lp, cp, n)
long *lp;
char *cp;

ltol3(cp, lp, n)
char *cp;
long *lp;
.fi
.ft R
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B l3tol
converts a list of
.I n
three-byte integers packed into a character string
pointed to by 
.I cp
into a list of long integers pointed to by
.IR lp .
.PP
.B ltol3
performs the inverse conversion from long integers
.RI ( lp )
to three-byte integers
.RI ( cp ).
.PP
These functions were used for file-system maintenance under
2.9BSD where disk addresses in inodes are three bytes long.
.SH SEE ALSO
fs(5)
.SH BUGS
.IR l3tol " and " ltol3
are present in 2.11BSD only for compatibility with 2.9BSD.  The functions are
deprecated and will be removed eventually.
